{"abstract":"As the development of new digital technologies is increasingly mobilised as a solution to global crises, such as in healthcare and the climate crisis, design is becoming an ever more influential actor in the legislation of answers to questions of ‘how to care’. This chapter explores the relationship between participatory design (PD) activities and care. We enquire empirically into how engagement and care are done in design practice by looking retrospectively at a PD project on welfare innovation for senior citizens in Denmark through the analytical lens of care. We draw on conceptions of care in the intersection of feminist research, science and technology studies (STS), and PD scholarships. Based on this, we develop the notion of ‘project engagement technologies’ (PET) as an analytical concept, which brings into view the role of material and technical entities that, despite their triviality, enable specific forms of engagement and care in design projects, and exclude others. We propose a view on attempts at doing ‘careful engagements’ as crafted activities and suggest PET as an empirical-ethnographic resource to critically examine conditions for engagement and care in projects and assemblages that aim to do ‘careful engagement’. We argue that since design and care are already deeply entangled in practice, and sometimes in problematic and uncareful ways, exploring relations between care and design may be an interesting topic for STS, opening new possibilities for intervention and fostering engagement and care through design.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Poderi, Giacomo","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Karasti, Helena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798521"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"project engagement technologies and their role in shaping conditions for engagement and care in participatory design projects","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-44119-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798521","identifier":[{"id":"85201998289","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0d795d6e-1fc9-48e6-871f-ffe793f42e5a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC6FBF1E4F83C60FB964634CB8E125FC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Giacomo","key":"poderipau","last":"Poderi","name":"Poderi, Giacomo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena","key":"karastipau","last":"Karasti","name":"Karasti, Helena","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Doris","key":"lydahlpedh","last":"Lydahl","name":"Lydahl, Doris","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Christian","key":"mossfeldtnickelsenpedh","last":"Mossfeldt Nickelsen","name":"Mossfeldt Nickelsen, Niels Christian","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-44119-6_2","eisbn":["9783031441196"],"isbn":["9783031441189"],"pages":"19-34","place":"Switzerland","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Ethical and Methodological Dilemmas in Social Science Interventions: Careful Engagements in Healthcare, Museums, Design and Beyond"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201998289"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0d795d6e-1fc9-48e6-871f-ffe793f42e5a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Project Engagement Technologies and Their Role in Shaping Conditions for Engagement and Care in Participatory Design Projects","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798521","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Voice-enabled technology has been celebrated as a breakthrough in eldercare. Mainstream discourses emphasize voice-based technology as practical assistants, and thus figure voice as a practical means to achieve certain ends. But there is more to voice interactions than merely distributing messages and articulating commands. Voice-based interactions create sonic environments, enact affect, identities, likes and dislikes. In this presentation we will explore the phenomenon of voice-based technology in the smart-home. Through ethnographic interviews we study how older people use voice-based technologies and with what effects for their experiences of the affective environment in their homes. We combine the concept from Science and Technology Studies of infrastructure with a cultural anthropological view on voice. Based on this, we see voice-based interactions as infrastructures that link the realms of the technical, cultural and sociopolitical to the level of the individual, creating sites where shared discourses and values, affect, and aesthetics are made manifest in and contested through embodied and material practice. The presentation makes audible interactions between voices, technologies, and homes, to exemplify some of the infrastructural and affective effects of voice-based technologies. We find that the use of voice-based technologies results in changes in the affective environments of the home, such as by creating uncertainty, harshness and intervening in cultural and temporal enactments of politeness. Moreover, their ability to make voices travel beyond the material confines of the home, renders its boundaries more permeable, thus creating a sense of disempowerment both towards technology and the management of the privacy of the home. We propose the phenomenon of voice and voice-enabled technologies as an interesting topic for socio-gerontechnology research.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718840"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective environment","Eldercare","Smart home infrastructure","Sonic interactions","Voice enabled technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voice based technology and ageing infrastructures of voice environments of affect","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718840","ids":["itu-356ce93d-d91f-45e4-b870-c0945278c73f"],"keyword":["- Affective environment","- Eldercare","- Smart-home infrastructure","- Sonic interactions","- Voice-enabled technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E24BA85805A531820E093F662B880ADE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-356ce93d-d91f-45e4-b870-c0945278c73f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voice-based Technology and Ageing : Infrastructures of Voice, Environments of Affect","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718840","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Nedlukningen af samfundet og risikoen for at blive smittet pga. COVID-19 pandemien betød, at mange ældre borgere blev socialt isolerede i store dele af 2020-2021. Men hvordan oplevede de ældre borgere selv den tvungne isolation og fysisk distancering? Artiklen baserer sig på et forskningsprojekt, der i 2020- 2021 gennemførte interviews med 20 alene-boende ældre borgere omkring deres hverdag under nedlukningen, oplevelsen af social isolation samt deres brug af digitale teknologier før og under nedlukningen. Historierne fra interviewene blandt ældre borgere giver et komplekst billede af deres oplevelse og kreativitet i forhold til at opretholde en hverdag under pande- mien. Derudover bidrager historierne til en mere nuanceret forståelse af spørgsmålet om, hvad socialitet er og kan være.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381348"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COVID 19 pandemic","Digital technology use","Older adults","Physical distancing","Social isolation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uden hverdagens møder men med tid til at puste ud historier om ældre menneskers hverdag under nedlukningen af samfundet","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92914244/gerontologi_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381348","ids":["itu-0627c0dd-258b-4005-af9f-b35528ec6ddc"],"keyword":["COVID-19 pandemic","Digital technology use","Older adults","Physical distancing","Social isolation"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6A7E800EA773DCDBCC8F342B37A4B3C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92914244/gerontologi_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16048644"],"issue":"2","journal":"Gerontologi","pages":"9-12","publisher":"University of Copenhagen","status":"p","title":"Gerontologi","volume":"38"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0627c0dd-258b-4005-af9f-b35528ec6ddc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uden hverdagens møder – men med tid til at puste ud : Historier om ældre menneskers hverdag under nedlukningen af samfundet.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381348","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Today, co-designing for social innovation is explored in many Western democracies to transform political agendas and develop sustainable societies. For social innovation to have a radical and wide-reaching impact on society, scaling is crucial. Scaling social innovation after ending a project requires a focus on making innovations sustainable in the long run and how they can foster organizational or institutional transformation. Despite increased interest in design for social innovation and scaling, little attention has been given to how the scaling of social innovation unfolds in practice over a longer period. A qualitative study was conducted following the continuation of a social innovation project called SeniorInteraction, which ended in 2012. Through interviews and field visits, we examined the attempts at scaling by different public and private partners and citizens after the project ended. The social innovation concept in question is an open exercise community in public parks for senior citizens supported by the local municipality. The research provides a deeper understanding of scaling in practice and identifies four important drivers for scaling social innovation: ownership, documentation, infrastructuring elements and rehearsing new practices. Additionally, we discuss challenges related to the way we understand and evaluate the scaling of social innovations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Brandt, Eva","Foverskov, Maria","Malmborg, Lone"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384632"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co design","Infrastructuring","Scaling","Social innovation","citizens driven services","public partnerships"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scaling social innovation ownership infrastructuring elements and rehearsing new practices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1386/art_00022_1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384632","identifier":[{"id":"85150641772","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e4b2d535-88df-4067-855a-91f8635654b3"],"keyword":["Scaling","citizens-driven services","co-design","infrastructuring","public partnerships","social Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7A06D31A971811825E30F651F7E48825"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/Scaling%20social%20innovation:%20Ownership,%20documentation,%20infrastructuring%20elements%20and%20rehearsing%20new%20practices","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://intellectdiscover.com/docserver/fulltext/ajdp/9/1-2/art.9.1-2.22.1_Yndigegn.pdf?expires=1675415095&id=id&accname=guest&checksum=2096FDA6D880AD75408AEB019A109E15","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1386/art_00022_1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"design school kolding","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-DSKD","l3nn":"Design School Kolding","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Design School Kolding","namevar":["Design School Kolding"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-DSKD","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1386/art_00022_1","issn":["17493463","17493471"],"issn_org":["17493463"],"journal":"Artifact: Journal of Design Practice","pages":"1","paperid":"22","publisher":"Intellect Books","status":"p","title":"Artifact: Journal of Design Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150641772"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e4b2d535-88df-4067-855a-91f8635654b3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Scaling social innovation: Ownership, infrastructuring elements and rehearsing new practices","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384632","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Developing primarily practice-oriented university courses for an online format challenges pedagogical ideas about learning communities, participation, and involvement in learning situations. Here, we report on a didactic design experiment, the aim of which was to design an online learning environment that supported practice-based learning and in which possibilities for participation were strengthened and expanded. The experiment was conducted during a 14-week university course on co-design, in which the teachers designed different digital tools and learning activities to strengthen the students’ feelings of belonging and community and student-to-student inspiration. The topics discussed in this paper include how to rethink teaching practices in relation to online digital learning spaces and—a new practice that emerged from the design experiment— how to create “in-between spaces.” These spaces can be considered slow spaces that support reflection and discussion, are less exposed, and can be created within and between lectures.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Gerwien, Rikke Gammeltoft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383095"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Online teaching","digital learning spaces","practice based learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"expanding possibilities for student participation in online learning environments for practice based teaching","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/lom.v15i26.130939","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383095","ids":["itu-7c7e68b5-84c6-43c6-bcd3-565783bd7c2c"],"keyword":["digital learning spaces","online teaching","practice-based learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5C66D14AC654709684C3C42AC8FC5682"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/lom.v15i26.130939","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92913807/Expanding_possibilities_for_student_participation_in_online_learning_environments_for_practice_based_teaching_4_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Gammeltoft","key":"gerwienpau","last":"Gerwien","name":"Gerwien, Rikke Gammeltoft","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/lom.v15i26.130939","issn":["1903248X"],"issue":"26","journal":"Læring og Medier","pages":"1-16","paperid":"1903-248X","publisher":"Statsbiblioteket","status":"p","title":"Læring og Medier","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7c7e68b5-84c6-43c6-bcd3-565783bd7c2c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Expanding possibilities for student participation in online learning environments for practice-based teaching","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383095","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Family members provide the majority of informal care for older adults in Sweden. Nevertheless, by providing a range of assistance, peers often emerge as a central to counter social isolation among older adults. Therefore, there is a need to know more about what informal care provision by older adults to their peers means for different groups of older adults. Aim: This study investigated the types of informal care and support that older adults provide to their peers in Sweden, and how these types of care and support are associated with demographic characteristics and social isolation. We also compared older adults who provide informal care and support with those who do not. Method: For this purpose, we used a national online survey named “Involuntary loneliness among senior citizens” answered by 10,044 older adults enrolled in the Swedish Citizen Panel. We adopted a mixed-method design to analyse the survey data, including free-text options (n = 2155) and numerical data. Social isolation was assessed using a score built from the social loneliness items of the UCLA Loneliness Scale. Results: In our population, 21.5% of the older adults were providing informal care and support to their peers. Practical/instrumental help was frequently offered by younger participants (<75 years), men and respondents who were less socially isolated. On a general level, the factors that were positively associated with giving informal care and support to peers were older age, being male, retired, married/living in a relationship, living in an urban area/big city and exhibiting greater isolation. Focusing specifically on social support shows that older participants (>80) and those experiencing less social isolation (score < 24) were more engaged in social activities. Conclusion: This paper is unique in exploring the informal peer-caregiver's perceptions of isolation. Data were collected during the COVID-19 pandemic; this highlights the need to recognise informal care and support between older adults and to acknowledge their contributions as an essential component of Swedish civil society, especially during a societal crisis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Siira, Elin","Olaya‐Contreras, Patricia","Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Wijk, Helle","Rolandsson, Bertil","Wolf, Axel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383115"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Informal care","Older adults","Peer support","Social isolation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"older adults provision of informal care and support to their peers a cornerstone of swedish society demographic characteristics and experiences of social isolation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/scs.13063","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383115","identifier":[{"id":"85122076485","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7e3561dd-0daa-4b16-abb3-04f6542a6fc9"],"keyword":["informal care","older adults","peer support","social isolation"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-06E7FB6D31A965AFC9A0E3A194FD40F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86616816/Scandinavian_Caring_Sciences_2022_Siira_Older_adults_provision_of_informal_care_and_support_to_their_peers_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/scs.13063","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/scs.13063","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elin","key":"siirapau","last":"Siira","name":"Siira, Elin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patricia","key":"olayacontreraspau","last":"Olaya‐Contreras","name":"Olaya‐Contreras, Patricia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"wijkpau","last":"Wijk","name":"Wijk, Helle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bertil","key":"rolandssonpau","last":"Rolandsson","name":"Rolandsson, Bertil","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, Axel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/scs.13063","issn":["02839318","14716712"],"issn_org":["02839318"],"journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Caring Sciences","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Caring Sciences","title_org":"Scandinavian journal of caring sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122076485"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7e3561dd-0daa-4b16-abb3-04f6542a6fc9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Older adults’ provision of informal care and support to their peers–A cornerstone of swedish society: : Demographic characteristics and experiences of social isolation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383115","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Voice-enabled technology has been celebrated as a breakthrough in eldercare. Mainstream discourses emphasize voice-based technology as practical assistants, and thus figure voice as a practical means to achieve certain ends. But there is more to voice interactions than merely distributing messages and articulating commands. Voice-based interactions create sonic environments, enact affect, identities, likes and dislikes. The paper explores the co-existence of older people and voice-based technologies ethnographically, and through the STS concept of infrastructure and a cultural anthropological view on voice. We see infrastructures as both objects and the relations between objects (Larkin), as ‘complex chains of material relations’ that ‘reconfigure bodies, societies [..] knowledge and discourses in ways often unnoticed’ (Harvey, Jensen and Morita). Voice is both a sonic material phenomenon and a culturally elaborated metaphor (Weidman), which connects deeply to feelings of intimacy, identity and community. Voice-based interactions can thus be seen as infrastructures that link the realms of the technical, cultural and sociopolitical to the level of the individual, creating sites where shared discourses and values, affect, and aesthetics are made manifest in and contested through embodied and material practice. With the increasing co-existence of older people and voice-based assistants, we see a need for ethnographic views on what these technologies are, how they can be studied, and what they do. We develop the notion of ‘infrastructures of voice and affect’ as a more-than-human approach to study entanglements of ageing, environments of affect and intimacy, and voice- based technology.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718859"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affect and intimacy","Ageing","Cultural anthropology","Eldercare","Ethnography","Infrastructures of voice","Material practices","Technocultural entanglements","Voice based interactions","Voice enabled technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructures of voice environments of affect amp intimacy voice based technology and older people","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718859","ids":["itu-62b8ea0d-ab92-471a-ae9e-02c05cb1aa1a"],"keyword":["Affect and intimacy","Ageing","Cultural anthropology","Eldercare","Ethnography","Infrastructures of voice","Material practices","Technocultural entanglements","Voice-based interactions","Voice-enabled technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C112D6973110624253D0A0B17232A5DD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-62b8ea0d-ab92-471a-ae9e-02c05cb1aa1a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructures of Voice, Environments of Affect &amp; Intimacy:  : Voice-based Technology and Older People","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718859","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper reflects on experiences with practicing and scaling a social innovation concept that was co-produced between public and private partners and citizens in a living design laboratory in Denmark from 2009-2012. The concept is a public service supporting ad-hoc exercise communities for senior citizens in public parks, based on playful activities. This paper builds upon follow-up studies which have been made since the project ended. We discuss how practicing the service unfolded over time, and how two municipalities have attempted scaling the concept. We deepen the understanding of theoretical concepts of scaling with experiences from practice by e.g., discussing ownership, exchanges between formal institutions and informal civic engagement, and a need for clarifying new roles and responsibilities.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Malmborg, Lone","Foverskov, Maria","Brandt, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736596"],"event":{"end":"2021-08-18","place":"Kolding, dk","start":"2021-08-15","title":"Nordes 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University, School of Arts and Communication (K3)"],"keyword":["Civic engagement","Ownership","Social innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond a living lab scaling social innovation","src":["arkk"],"src-code":["DI-ART-DSKD"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2021.36","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-736596","ids":["arkk-603d159b-2c8b-45af-bed3-a4561aeebd55"],"keyword":["Ad-hoc exercise community","Living Laboratory","Scaling social innovation","Social Innovation","Yes","civic engagement","ownership","public and private partners"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8DE3582B0208EE856768ED32FF9BA3CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2021.36","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"malmö university school of arts and communication","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University, School of Arts and Communication (K3)","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"design school kolding","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-DSKD","l3nn":"Design School Kolding","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Design School Kolding","namevar":["Design School Kolding"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-DSKD","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"4186dd98-15a8-4d67-a630-5d0875e85920","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpedh","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"markussenpedh","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Thomas","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eeva","key":"berglundpedh","last":"Berglund","name":"Berglund, Eeva","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guy","key":"julierpedh","last":"Julier","name":"Julier, Guy","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"lindepedh","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Per","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/nordes.2021.36","eisbn":["16049705"],"pages":"328-337","status":"p","subtitle":"Matters of Scale","title":"Proceedings of the 9th Nordic Design Research Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkk-603d159b-2c8b-45af-bed3-a4561aeebd55"],"src":["Design School Kolding"],"title":"Beyond a Living Lab: Scaling Social Innovation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-736596","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper reflects on experiences with practicing and scaling a social innovation concept that was co-produced between public and private partners and citizens in a living design laboratory in Denmark from 2009-2012. The concept is a public service supporting ad-hoc exercise communities for senior citizens in public parks, based on playful activities. This paper builds upon follow-up studies which have been made since the project ended. We discuss how practicing the service unfolded over time, and how two municipalities have attempted scaling the concept. We deepen the understanding of theoretical concepts of scaling with experiences from practice by e.g., discussing ownership, exchanges between formal institutions and informal civic engagement, and a need for clarifying new roles and responsibilities.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Malmborg, Lone","Foverskov, Maria","Brandt, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747260"],"event":{"acronym":"Nordes","title":"Nordic Design Research Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Ad hoc Exercise Communities","Living Design Laboratory","Public private partnership","Scaling Public Services","Social innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond a living lab scaling social innovation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://archive.nordes.org/index.php/n13/article/viewFile/601/568","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747260","ids":["itu-b9118579-adff-4e50-bf54-c7ed87e5276c"],"keyword":["Ad-hoc Exercise Communities","Living Design Laboratory","Public-Private Partnership","Scaling Public Services","Social Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-26BD449B0365549BA51B50070BCC2009"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://archive.nordes.org/index.php/n13/article/viewFile/601/568","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"design school kolding","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-DSKD","l3nn":"Design School Kolding","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Design School Kolding","namevar":["Design School Kolding"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-DSKD","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"328","place":"Kolding","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 9th Nordic Design Research Conference, Kolding, Denmark","title":"Matters of Scale"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b9118579-adff-4e50-bf54-c7ed87e5276c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beyond a Living Lab: Scaling Social Innovation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747260","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383718"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital marginalisering af udsatte ældre arbejdsrapport","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383718","ids":["itu-a86968c7-85c0-463a-8ebe-ba3c550f9556"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3675A6515EE709CAD989AD86C7298D1A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a86968c7-85c0-463a-8ebe-ba3c550f9556"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital marginalisering af udsatte ældre : Arbejdsrapport","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Voice-enabled technology has been seen as a breakthrough in eldercare, as practical assistants, and as social companions for older people. While dominant innovation discourses articulate these technologies as means to an end, research based on sociotechnical understandings has shown how technology, ageing and care cannot be seen as separate from each other, but as co-constituted (Peine et al., 2021). Building on this view, and through a focus on sociotechnical imaginaries we explore how voice-enabled technologies are slowly beginning to transform care, ageing and the home, as they are increasingly pervading public, political and corporate discourses, and put into use in the homes and everyday practices of older people. Sociotechnical imaginaries are, drawing on Jasanoff’s definition; “collectively held, publicly performed visions of desirable futures, animated by shared understandings of forms of social life, and social order attainable through, and supportive of, advances in science and technology” (Jasanoff 2015, 19). Sociotechnical imaginaries are at once descriptive of attainable futures and prescriptive of the kinds of futures that ought to be attained. This paper explores how sociotechnical imaginaries of voice-enabled technologies, ageing and care are being co-constituted in different sites through analyses of documents and visual representations, and ethnographic studies with older people using voice-enabled technologies. We look at big tech companies’ imaginaries of ageing and care vis a vis voice-enabled technologies, and explore how such imaginaries are being performed and negotiated in interactions between older people and voice-based technologies. The paper contributes to the philosophy of technology by giving empirical examples of how concrete voice-enabled technologies take part in forming sociotechnical imaginaries and futures of ageing, care and the home.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Ertner, Sara Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677310"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ageing","Eldercare","Philosophy of technology","Sociotechnical imaginaries","Voice enabled technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voice enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care ageing and the home voice enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care ageing and the home","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.2021spt.com/abstracts/Book_of_abstracts_rl2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677310","ids":["itu-4bef3484-779b-41a2-b32b-9db20db9e659"],"keyword":["Ageing","Eldercare","Philosophy of technology","Sociotechnical imaginaries","Voice-enabled technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-61E3088AED515718EE2104AA68EEE11B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.2021spt.com/abstracts/Book_of_abstracts_rl2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4bef3484-779b-41a2-b32b-9db20db9e659"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voice-enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care, ageing and the home : Voice-enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care, ageing and the home","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677310","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This study analyzes the co-production of peer-to-peer interactions as a social innovation that utilizes older people’s resources as a means for providing public care. We ethnographically explore an initiative named Give&Take that aims to establish peer-to-peer care among older people. We draw on a practice perspective with respect to care and its organization while also being influenced by the conceptualization of sociomateriality. The study illustrates the co-production of peer-to-peer care within a social innovation at the intersection of formal and informal care. We show how care practices and their specificities clash with institutionalized logics in the co-production of care. In conclusion, we argue that considering how care practices are shaped by a set of institutionalized logics in public innovations enhances our understanding of the coproduction of care that draws on older people’s resources. These findings are of importance to innovations following EU policies on co-production and active aging.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677321"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aging","Care practices","Ethnography","Sociomateriality","peer to peer care"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co production of peer to peer care practices the case of a social innovation in elderly care","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.tecnoscienza.net/index.php/tsj/article/view/447","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677321","identifier":[{"id":"85150625067","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7dc60851-ce15-451b-98c3-18b391a7f11d"],"keyword":["aging","care practices","ethnography","peer-to-peer care","sociomateriality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B5B7CA6512A524643530A1DACC9A7A48"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.tecnoscienza.net/index.php/tsj/article/view/447","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["20383460"],"issue":"2","journal":"Tecnoscienza: Italian Journal of Science & Technology Studies","pages":"73","publisher":"STS Italia - The Italian Society of Science and Technology Studies","status":"p","title":"Tecnoscienza: Italian Journal of Science & Technology Studies","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150625067"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7dc60851-ce15-451b-98c3-18b391a7f11d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-production of Peer-to-Peer Care Practices. : The Case of a Social Innovation in Elderly Care","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677321","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Loneliness among elderly is articulated as a major problem. Loneliness is compared to smoking as a health problem that is fatal. Therefore, in recent years, large pools of funding have been allocated to support various projects that work to solve or reduce the articulated problem of too many lonely elderly. Loneliness is articulated as a social problem but also a problem that can be solved. The initiatives taken to solve the problem are often governed by an activation and/or socialization agenda. But what is loneliness, where is loneliness and is loneliness a problem that can be solved or at least reduced from public institutional side? This paper examines how loneliness among elderly are articulated among public institutions and other organizations that work with elderly healthcare - and how initiatives to solve the problem are done. Loneliness is something that is difficult to grasp, while it is something everyone to some extend knows the feeling of. Loneliness among elderly is posed as a societal problem at a time where there is cut backs on elderly care. Time and number of hands that can be used in elderly care are reduced - and at the same time, caregivers are thought in many situations as an important tool in solving loneliness as a problem. The caregivers are already ‘out there’, so they can be used to identify where the problem is - and at the same time communicate possible solution e.g. propose initiatives to the citizens for which the citizen can participate. Based on studies of policy documents and reports - and ethnographic observations of caregivers and volunteers I ask what is loneliness in this institutionalized problematization and what definition of loneliness are inscribed into the different initiatives, tools and technologies that seek to solve or reduce the problem?","author_count":1,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384301"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Caregiver roles in elderly care","Elderly healthcare","Institutional approaches to loneliness","Loneliness among elderly","Socialization initiatives"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what is loneliness the different articulation of loneliness among elderly in problematizations as well as solution oriented initiatives","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384301","ids":["itu-cefcb6a7-6e1d-4281-8b42-49b1ae685538"],"keyword":["Caregiver roles in elderly care","Elderly healthcare","Institutional approaches to loneliness","Loneliness among elderly","Socialization initiatives"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4647D529D4475FA817FEFB8630EE944C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cefcb6a7-6e1d-4281-8b42-49b1ae685538"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What is loneliness? : The different articulation of loneliness among elderly in problematizations as well as solution-oriented initiatives?","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384301","year":"2018","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This workshop invites participatory design (PD) researchers and practitioners to consider and exchange experiences of controversies and agonism in codesign projects with citizens and various public partners. Many public actors like departments and other units in county and city councils, municipalities, hospitals etc. are entering codesign projects as a way of engaging citizens or patients in social, urban or medical innovation projects. Often private actors are also part of these partnerships forming the so-called quadruple helix partnerships. While codesign approaches do indeed present new possibilities for the development of interesting and sustainable design innovations we have often experienced controversies and agonism caused by for instance different political agendas, beliefs and values among the participants. This workshop will focus on sharing of and reflection on challenges of navigating between diverging opinions, political agendas and values of citizens and professional public actors in codesign projects. We will discuss how to navigate in such quadruple helix partnerships while doing PD projects as democratic processes. The outcome of the workshop is a large poster visualizing a landscape with specific examples of controversies and agonism, including identification of the roles of essential socio-material collectives of humans and non-humans and reflections on tactics and strategies for how to handle specific situations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Malmborg, Lone","Brandt, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-126507"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-24","place":"Hasselt & Genk, be","start":"2018-08-20","title":"Participatory Design Conference 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Codesign","Democracy","Participatory Design","Politics","Power","Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"codesigning with public partners controversies and agonism","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3210604.3210651","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-126507","identifier":[{"id":"85055510225","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-36952873-51d9-4c74-8376-ee3522212215"],"keyword":["No","Participatory Design","codesign","democracy","politics","power","research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-18AF0036AE69374781A9D342254E285D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3210604.3210651","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Design, Institute of Design and Visual Interaction","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Design, Institute of Design and Visual Interaction, CODE - Centre for Codesign","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"4186dd98-15a8-4d67-a630-5d0875e85920","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3210604.3210651","isbn":["9781450355742"],"place":"Hasselt, Genk, Belgium","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the participatory Design Conference 2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055510225"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-36952873-51d9-4c74-8376-ee3522212215"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Codesigning with public partners: Controversies and agonism","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-126507","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"There are few examples of academic work that describe Participatory Design (PD) and Co-design instruction. This paper presents experiences from four years of teaching a university course on Co-design and PD to an average of 57 students per year. A main part of our pedagogical approach is the implementation of Donald Schön’s concept of a reflective practicum, via a mandatory ‘live’ project that runs for the whole semester. We discuss the potential and challenges of teaching PD and Co-design to large classes using live projects, including how to give students first-hand experience of the whole PD process, how to coach students in collecting and using field data, and what expectations of a Co-design process and its participants are realistic. The paper also examines how PD-related challenges affect teaching PD as an academic subject.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Messeter, Jörn","Grönvall, Erik","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382167"],"event":{"acronym":"PDC","title":"Participatory Design Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Analysis","Co design","Lessons learnt","Live projects","Participatory Design","Reflections","Teaching","University course"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"teaching participatory design using live projects critical reflections and lessons learnt","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83392524/PDC2018_teachingPD_FINAL_18052018_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382167","ids":["itu-3cf1ce47-12ed-4ffe-95e8-002b4382b378"],"keyword":["Analysis","Co-design","Lessons learnt","Live projects","Participatory Design","Reflections","Teaching","University course"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F35BC0DC0DBA570BAD0CFBED3A62A093"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83392524/PDC2018_teachingPD_FINAL_18052018_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"christianssonpau","last":"Christiansson","locid":"a4c1604d-b01f-46ef-baf3-74d2a8046d6b","name":"Messeter, Jörn","name_org":"Christiansson, Jörn","orcid":"0000-0002-2181-149X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3210586.3210597","isbn":["9781450363716"],"issn":["21505896"],"pages":"1-11","place":"New York, US","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference","status":"p","title":"PDC '18 Proceedings of the 15th Participatory Design Conference : Full papers - Volume 1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3cf1ce47-12ed-4ffe-95e8-002b4382b378"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Teaching Participatory Design using Live Projects: Critical Reflections and Lessons Learnt","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382167","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Designing participation over time is a challenge that is regularly discussed in the fields of Participatory Design (PD) and Codesign. This paper describes two living labs-cases concerned with designing IT during long-term engagements with communities. Both labs aim to enable participatory exchanges after the designer leaves and are thus confronted with challenges that transcend the time of the traditional design ‘project’. We addressed these challenges via defining the IT design process as scripting, which is a process that better articulates the participants’ different voices and timelines. In this process three types of scripts are made, supported by the facilitator role: personal scripts as portrayals of individuals’ views on issues in the community and timelines to address these; community scripts aspiring to combine personal scripts into pluralistic views on the community and scripts for action as ways to rehearse how the community might unfold after the designer leaves. Key to this approach is that diverse people’s views and timelines play a role in co-constructing IT platforms that support participation in the community over time. By creating IT tools that are enabled by and support scripting, designing for participation over time becomes a pluralistic endeavour.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Huybrechts, Liesbeth","Hendriks, Niels","Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Malmborg, Lone"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383085"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hasselt University","Social Spaces, LUCA School of Arts"],"keyword":["Codesign","Participatory Design","Scripting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scripting an exploration of designing for participation over time with communities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82498440/Scripting_an_exploration_of_designing_for_participation_over_time_with_communities_CoDesign_Vol_14_No_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383085","identifier":[{"id":"85041138650","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7b9732ba-f3dc-4100-be0c-027cd975a4e5"],"keyword":["Participatory design","codesign","scripting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-37840E7E7B9523057E263A2E6A292610"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82498440/Scripting_an_exploration_of_designing_for_participation_over_time_with_communities_CoDesign_Vol_14_No_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"hasselt university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasselt University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"social spaces luca school of arts","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Social Spaces, LUCA School of Arts","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liesbeth","key":"huybrechtspau","last":"Huybrechts","name":"Huybrechts, Liesbeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"hendrikspau","last":"Hendriks","name":"Hendriks, Niels","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/15710882.2018.1424205","issn":["15710882","17453755"],"issn_org":["15710882"],"issue":"1","journal":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","pages":"17-31","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041138650"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7b9732ba-f3dc-4100-be0c-027cd975a4e5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Scripting: an exploration of designing for participation over time with communities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383085","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Living labs are increasingly used as an approach for facilitating innovation and testing emerging information technologies. In this paper we analyse three large-scale technology design projects in Danish healthcare where co-design and implementation activities were organised in living labs. We describe some of the critical challenges that we experienced from transitioning technology prototypes and co-design activities into becoming part of the daily lives of patients, citizens and healthcare practitioners. The main challenges relate to creating and sustaining new work practices, scaling the number of participants, and facilitating the transition between everyday life and living lab behaviour.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Tariq Osman","Kanstrup, Anne Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-406556"],"event":{"acronym":"SHI","end":"2018-08-29","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2018-08-28","title":"16th Scandinavian Conference on Health Informatics 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"three living labs in denmark challenges with co design and implementation of health it","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-406556","ids":["ku-15faf2eb-6d65-4eca-a6fd-be0372121069"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-008CC7F0B249E6E8081A3E76CC8E11A2"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tariq Osman","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"dfc4b3ec-64f4-4e84-92fe-67e3b681c85b","name":"Andersen, Tariq Osman","orcid":"0000-0002-9342-5520","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Marie","key":"kanstruppau","last":"Kanstrup","name":"Kanstrup, Anne Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789176852132"],"issn":["16503740"],"pages":"1-6","publisher":"Linköping University Electronic Press","series":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings from The 16th Scandinavian Conference on Health Informatics 2018,"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-15faf2eb-6d65-4eca-a6fd-be0372121069"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Three living labs in Denmark : Challenges with co-design and implementation of health IT","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-406556","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Living labs are increasingly used as an approach for facilitating innovation and testing emerging information technologies. In this paper we analyse three large-scale technology design projects in Danish healthcare where co-design and implementation activities were organised in living labs. We describe some of the critical challenges that we experienced from transitioning technology prototypes and co-design activities into becoming part of the daily lives of patients, citizens and healthcare practitioners. The main challenges relate to creating and sustaining new work practices, scaling the number of participants, and facilitating the transition between everyday life and living lab behaviour.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Osman Andersen, Tariq","Kanstrup, Anne Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S02-086.67-005145"],"event":{"acronym":"SHI","end":"2018-08-29","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2018-08-28","title":"Scandinavian Conference on Health Informatics","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Co design","Healthcare innovation","Living labs","Technology implementation","Work practice transformation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"three living labs in denmark challenges with co design and implementation of health it","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84077336/Three_Living_Labs_in_Denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.67-005145","ids":["aau-6a288925-7656-4bbd-8b0d-72ed4bd6db6e","itu-acee5489-bace-4b15-a204-30223e4a980a"],"keyword":["Co-design","Healthcare inn