{"abstract":"In this paper, we discuss two emerging controversies in the meeting between participatory design (PD) ideals and the funding regime in an EU-funded cross-sector partnership project with seven partners. We argue that this discussion is much needed within the PD community, as more and more research is funded through outlets that challenge current design practices in PD that emphasize bottom-up and open-ended processes. We argue for a continued need for reflexive PD practices that take implications of publicly funded cross-sector partnerships into account.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Holdgaard, Nanna","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382468"],"event":{"acronym":"PDC","title":"Participatory Design Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross sector partnership","EU funded projects","Participatory Design","funding regime","reflexive practices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"participatory design negotiations in project funding regimes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83425094/a15_holdgaard.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382468","identifier":[{"id":"85055497899","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5036fded-06da-4ba9-8660-38b8601f3ce7"],"keyword":["EU-funded projects","cross-sector partnership","funding regime","participatory design","reflexive practices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1BDC5A83AACBEBAE28540767913C9599"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83425094/a15_holdgaard.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"holdgaardpau","last":"Holdgaard","name":"Holdgaard, Nanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3210604.3210647","eisbn":["9781450355742/18/08"],"issn":["21505896"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference","status":"p","subtitle":"Short Papers, Situated Actions, Workshops and Tutorial - Volume 2","title":"PDC '18 Proceedings of the 15th Participatory Design Conference","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055497899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5036fded-06da-4ba9-8660-38b8601f3ce7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Participatory Design – Negotiations in Project Funding Regimes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382468","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Time is a matter of great concern to healthcare and eldercare. In situations of austerity, time is both an essential resource and an issue – what to spend time on? how to save time? Care and innovation both consume time, but they are also practices that generate (or assemble) time in different ways. This paper explores the different ways of assembling ageing, time, technology and care in differently located practices; a Danish innovation project aiming at developing technologies for older people, and a Danish home care unit seeking to implement new technologies of care. Drawing on empirical observations of the controversies emerging around time and technology, we inquire into the ontology of time. Performative approaches to care and innovation have asked questions about the socio-material nature of things like technology, bodies, disease and care. In this paper we engage with the materiality of time, and ask how different material practices perform time in different ways. Based on ethnographic observations of controversies around time in practices of eldercare and innovation we ask what kind of a thing is time? Technologies for care-work promise to save and recover time, but, we contend, they also change what time is, which creates controversies when implemented in practice where other types of time prevail.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382606"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ageing","CARE","Innovation","Technology","Time"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"matters of time the different times of technological innovation and care practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382606","ids":["itu-5a453ef8-163c-413e-acc0-6fa6df15f09c"],"keyword":["Ageing","Care","Innovation","Time","technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-80A37543C14AB3DA8BE396F98D580176"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5a453ef8-163c-413e-acc0-6fa6df15f09c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Matters of time : the different times of technological innovation and care practice.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382606","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Citizen engagement and the citizens as a resource are key concepts in rethinking the Danish welfare system to meet the challenges of delivering better services for the elderly, while simultaneously reducing the cost of healthcare. In this method paper, we address how the co-design of new digital service platforms takes place in the format of living labs. We characterize living labs as the design of experiential spaces where ‘what is’ and ‘what could be’ are explored over a longer period of engagement. The labs are staged to integrate multiple stakeholders’ issues and resources and to create new technologies, concepts, or service designs. This paper unpacks the practices of living labs with questions of what is being produced, not only in terms of products, but also in terms of changes in practices, roles, and relations. To analyze and discuss this question the authors report about their engagement in two co-design projects that focus on a digitally mediated community practice of sharing and exchanging.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe","Aakjær, Marie Kirstejn"],"cuid":["S02-082.50-038323"],"event":{"acronym":"PIN-C","end":"2018-01-13","place":"Västerås","start":"2018-01-11","title":"Partecipatori Innovation Conference","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Citizen engagement","Co design","Danish welfare system","Digital service platforms","Living labs","management organizational development and innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"living lab format for rehearsing a new service practice","src":["itu","pha"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84144087/track_2c_yndigegn_p111_119.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.50-038323","ids":["itu-716ad4b2-872b-4e76-a697-1ef503401953","pha-34919600-c915-4baa-b8a9-de38baa78750"],"keyword":["Citizen engagement","Co-design","Danish welfare system","Digital service platforms","Living labs","management, organizational development and innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-5FA4E0F9F26182E180CAA0E9B40596A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84144087/track_2c_yndigegn_p111_119.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pin-c.sdu.dk/assets/track-2c-yndigegn-p111-119.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Absalon - Ledelse og organisering af velfærdsinnovation","Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Center for Ledelse og Organisering - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Kirstejn","key":"aakjærpau","last":"Aakjær","locid":"f12dfe36-dd29-4812-80fa-51454a18dcec","name":"Aakjær, Marie Kirstejn","orcid":"0000-0003-0990-4201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"111-119","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Participatory Innovation Conference, Eskilstuna 2018","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-716ad4b2-872b-4e76-a697-1ef503401953","pha-34919600-c915-4baa-b8a9-de38baa78750"],"src":["AB University College Absalon","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Living Lab: Format for rehearsing a new (service) practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.50-038323","year":2018,"yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"In the Give&Take project, work package 3 has been the framework for collaborative explorations of sharing communities primarily among seniors through design laboratories and living labs. Senior communities, municipal institutions, NGO’s and their employees in Vienna, Austria and in Frederiksberg, Denmark have been engaged in codesigning and cocreating digital sharing platforms and in exploring and evaluating these platforms and the associated everyday practices in close collaboration with project partners. In this deliverable that consists of (1) a brief overview of emergent practices, (2) three printed magazines that document different aspects of these practices, (3) a workshop game that provides a structured approach for municipalities and others to evaluate the relevance of the Give&Take Platform, (4) an overview of living lab uses cases and (5) video documentation from the 11 living labs established through the project, the outcomes of work package 3 are presented and discussed with an emphasis on how to take the Give&Take platform further beyond the termination of the project.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Malmborg, Lone","Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Brandt, Eva","Foverskov, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730187"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative design","Digital platforms","Living labs","Senior engagement","Sharing communities"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"documenting emerging practices incl appendices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103512435/D3.4_Documenting_emerging_practices_incl_appendices.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This publication has been produced with the assistance of the European Union under the AAL Joint Programme. The content of this publication is the sole responsibility of the Give&Take consortium and can in no way be taken to reflect the views of the European Union."],"id":"S01-000.00-730187","ids":["itu-a37cb8a1-f675-456e-8e60-08fb13948ef4"],"keyword":["Collaborative design","Digital platforms","Living labs","Senior engagement","Sharing communities"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-80461C13C4202D91A1781324C862E0C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103512437/D2.3_RevisedServiceExchangeModel.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103512441/D5.5_Release_candidate.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103512439/D1.1_Project_Website.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103512435/D3.4_Documenting_emerging_practices_incl_appendices.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103512443/D5.6_Quality_assurance_report.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a37cb8a1-f675-456e-8e60-08fb13948ef4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Documenting emerging practices incl appendices","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730187","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This dissertation is a retrospective reflection on a user-driven innovation project, Senior Interaktion. The project was a three-year long project with focus on how to design services for senior citizens and to do that with a co-design approach involving citizens and private partners in the design work. The aim was to design services for senior citizens with the focus on social interaction – and with technology as a way to support the interaction among communities of elderlies. The dissertation is a retrospective reflection of the author’s experience with taking part and being heavily involved as participant in this project. This is done through a series of selected “moments” from the project and beyond, which in various ways are significant for what is happening in the project – and how the project is enacted. The dissertation contains of two research aims. The first is concerned with resistance as part of co-design and citizen involvement with the aim to reflect upon something that is rarely described or discussed within co-design and participatory design. The question is here how resistance is performed in practice, especially in the meetings between citizens and the project, and how resistance is handled in the project, or not handled. One of the arguments here is that the project overlooks the resistance toward the project itself, which means it doesn’t get to challenge the overall frame. The second part is concerned with the complexities of the ‘what’ and ‘where’ of living labs. The aim is here to describe and reflect upon what is being performed in the living lab, as this rather new practice within co-design and participatory design lacks empirical descriptions – but also with the intention to contribute to the discussion of co-design in “new” constellations of multiple partners and multiple organizations. The loose set-up of the living lab and these project constellations raise questions of who is working for whom, who owns it, who is responsible - but also questions of who knows the rules and terms of conditions. The dissertation ends with a discussion of the issues raised throughout the dissertation and a suggestion of an alternative that is about wanting something with each other.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382142"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing resistance and negotiating co design reflections on troublesome and elusive moments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109064747/PhD_Thesis_Signe_Louise_Yndigegn.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382142","ids":["itu-3bdb0898-84bc-4e87-906b-08c31d897f5e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5E1EF6D6EFC0BE9F9BDA30E44B8D37FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109064747/PhD_Thesis_Signe_Louise_Yndigegn.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779493391"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"120","pages":"207","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3bdb0898-84bc-4e87-906b-08c31d897f5e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Managing resistance and negotiating co-design : Reflections on troublesome and elusive moments","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382142","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
